From f8a5ca9cff7843606a6f73ea8b8891538d7e8d78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 01:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] security: apply deep audit fixes - JWT, rate limiting,
 must_change_password, org-override logging, file upload limits, SMS send
 logging, missing indexes, onboarding token bug

- CRITICAL: JWT_SECRET now fails hard if unset or <32 chars (no more hardcoded fallback)
- CRITICAL: must_change_password enforced server-side in deps.py (blocks all non-auth endpoints)
- CRITICAL: hardcoded super-admin email removed from main.py -> uses SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL env var
- HIGH: brute-force rate limiting on /auth/login (10 failures per 15 min per IP+email)
- HIGH: X-Org-Override now emits structured audit log entry on every use
- BUG: onboarding register passed dict to create_access_token(User) - fixed with db.refresh(user)
- BUG: send_sms() never created Message row or returned Message object - fixed; now logs and returns
- SECURITY: file upload endpoints validate extension (.xlsx/.xls/.csv only) and cap at 50MB
- SECURITY: password minimum length standardized to 8 chars across all endpoints (was 6 in one place)
- PERF: added 3 missing DB indexes on leads (org+advisor, org+source_file, org+channel+status)
- SECURITY: SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL and BOOKING_SECRET added to render.yaml env var declarations
- NOTE: BOOKING_SECRET still has a weak fallback in sms_service.py for local dev; set in Render

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01De8hPPn7iSWhtv1QoAnWSA
