From 83e3abd4cff574afb97e26ebe7e7d152377b4520 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 01:39:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] =?UTF-8?q?security:=20fix=2010=20more=20audit=20findi?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ngs=20=E2=80=94=20broken=20admin=20check,=20hardcoded=20key,=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?open=20redirect,=20XSS,=20prompt=20injection,=20rate=20limiting?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- crm_router: _require_admin used nonexistent is_admin/is_super_admin attributes,
  causing AttributeError 500 on every admin CRM endpoint and silently bypassing
  all access control. Fixed to check current_user.role against ('org_admin','super_admin').
- setup_router: SECRET_KEY fell back to hardcoded 'changeme' when env var missing.
  Now raises RuntimeError at startup if neither SECRET_KEY nor JWT_SECRET is set/valid.
- email_tracking_router: /click/{id} was an unauthenticated open redirect — any
  url param was redirected unconditionally, including javascript:/data: schemes.
  Now validates scheme is http/https before redirecting.
- campaign_router: /builder/send allowed any advisor (not just admins) to trigger
  a bulk SMS campaign to all org leads. Changed dependency to require_admin.
- concierge_router: public AI chat had no rate limiting, no message-count cap,
  no per-message size limit, and accepted arbitrary role values including 'system'
  (prompt injection). Added per-IP rate limiter (30 req/60s), max 20 messages,
  2000 char per message, role restricted to Literal['user','assistant'].
- survey_router: org_name, first_name injected into HTML without html.escape()
  (stored XSS). brand_color_primary injected raw into CSS (CSS injection).
  Social URLs embedded in href without scheme validation (javascript: XSS).
  Fixed with html.escape(), _safe_color() hex validator, _safe_url() scheme check.
- fiber_intake_router: org_name injected into HTML page title, consent text,
  and thank-you page without escaping (stored XSS). Fixed with html.escape().
- settings_router: social link and booking_page URL fields accepted javascript:
  scheme (stored XSS). Profile photo accepted image/svg+xml data URLs (stored XSS
  via SVG script). Added _validate_url() http/https guard and tightened photo
  MIME regex to jpeg/png/gif/webp only.
- org_settings_router: same javascript: URL risk on org-level social links endpoint.
  Added _validate_url() with http/https enforcement.
- cadence_template_router: /seed-defaults was open to any authenticated advisor
  (writes template rows to DB). Changed to require_admin.
