From 19d2c74657ea8f8c68d631c2e5afde88290f8692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 01:41:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] security: fix cross-org Lead queries, raw exception leak,
 Meta/TikTok webhook HMAC, admin dep pattern
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- pipeline_router: Lead lookups in get_flagged, approve_flagged, get_conversations
  were missing organization_id scope — cross-org lead data could leak if a
  PipelineConversation.lead_id ever referenced a foreign lead. Added org scope.
  Also replaced detail=str(e) (raw exception in HTTP response) with a generic
  message; actual error is now logged server-side.
- reports_router: User query in revenue_by_period was missing organization_id filter
  — advisors from other orgs could appear in the by-advisor sales breakdown if
  outcome.recorded_by_id crossed org boundaries. Added org scope.
- availability_router: Lead lookup in get_upcoming_appointments was missing
  organization_id scope. Added scope matching the booking's advisor's org.
- social_webhooks_router: Meta webhook had no HMAC signature verification —
  any caller knowing the org_token could inject arbitrary fake leads. Added
  X-Hub-Signature-256 verification using org.meta_app_secret (warns if secret
  not yet configured). TikTok webhook previously silently skipped HMAC when
  tiktok_webhook_secret was unset; now rejects with 403 and an error log.
  Also fixed get_or_create_webhook_token to use require_admin as a proper
  FastAPI Depends() rather than an inline function call.
---
